{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/525271-some-questions-concerning-tells","id":525271,"title":"Some Questions Concerning Tells","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-23T01:41:48-07:00","id":525271,"title":"Some Questions Concerning Tells","content":"I'm sure that I'll have more of these, eventually, but I'm just going to start with the one. (Though this might be a good place to keep others!)<br /> <br /> So, first up is the Exciting Tell. This seems like a neat power, which backs up a lot of the mythos behind werewolves. There are a few things missing from it, however.<br /> <br /> It says that the power works when sweat is exchanged, but doesn't say much beyond that. Being a supernatural ability, I would assume that this isn't some sort of biochemical pheremonal issue that's going on with it right? It's actual magic?<br /> <br /> So then would this power work against something like vampires? <br /> <br /> Technically, vampires don't sweat. They could in theory absorb sweat, though, and have it trigger that way. But again, being a supernatural power, is the actual exchange of sweat the mechanic, or just a condition that causes the power to activate?<br /> <br /> TL;DR - Does Exciting work on Vampires?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5309-chancetr","name":"ChanceTR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5309_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T01:53:00-07:00","id":525293,"title":"","content":"I think that was just poetic. As long as you're exerting yourself and touch I think it should work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T07:26:28-07:00","id":525452,"title":"","content":"ST call. I would not have it work on vampires, but I don't think you'd be wrong for ruling that it does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T20:59:11-07:00","id":528462,"title":"","content":"Alright. I was hoping for something a bit more definite, but that's cool too. Part 2 of this question:<br /> <br /> How long does this 'addiction' last? Just until they lose willpower once, or does it continue on after that? It doesn't say that it applies the addicted condition, but it also doesn't really talk about how it's resolved after it's started, if the Wolf-Blood is unwilling to engage or unable to engage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5309-chancetr","name":"ChanceTR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5309_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T09:56:57-07:00","id":528901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The next time the character who isn\u2019t the Wolf-Blooded can share the same experience, no matter how inconvenient it might be, they must, or lose a point of Willpower until the Wolf-Blooded again willingly engages in the activity. </div> </div> </div>Seems pretty straightforward to me, could you be more specific about where the confusion lies?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T12:32:34-07:00","id":529128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/525271-some-questions-concerning-tells?p=528901#post528901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seems pretty straightforward to me, could you be more specific about where the confusion lies?</div> </div> </div> </div>He's wondering if he should treat it's effects like a persistent addition condition. Reading it like that, the drawback only applies once until such a time where the behavior is resisted, thus negating Willpower once. A relapse is a possibility, after that..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T01:22:10-07:00","id":529677,"title":"","content":"That is what I was wondering, yes. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It says that it's addictive, but it doesn't apply the addicted condition, or really have any mechanics other than 'if you have the opportunity to do it and can't, or the wolf-blood won't, you lose a point of willpower''. It doesn't say anything about how long that goes on for, etc.<br /> <br /> As a side note: It seems like this would be better as a Condition with a specific resolution, rather than just kind of free-floating mechanics like that.<br /> <br /> But, Ephsy pretty much nailed the question I had. I was wondering if this was a persistent loss, or just a one-off thing. If it's one point of willpower and bang, cured, that seems reasonable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5309-chancetr","name":"ChanceTR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5309_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T07:48:14-07:00","id":529953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChanceTR</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/525271-some-questions-concerning-tells?p=529677#post529677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is what I was wondering, yes. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It says that it's addictive, but it doesn't apply the addicted condition, or really have any mechanics other than 'if you have the opportunity to do it and can't, or the wolf-blood won't, you lose a point of willpower''. It doesn't say anything about how long that goes on for, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does, it says &quot;the next time&quot;. So, the time after next? Presumably you wouldn't have to spend Willpower to resist that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChanceTR</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/525271-some-questions-concerning-tells?p=529677#post529677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a side note: It seems like this would be better as a Condition with a specific resolution, rather than just kind of free-floating mechanics like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I very much agree. And I think the Addicted Condition is a good replacement for this mechanic, just have it resolve when they indulge the addiction instead of being Persistent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChanceTR</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/525271-some-questions-concerning-tells?p=529677#post529677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But, Ephsy pretty much nailed the question I had. I was wondering if this was a persistent loss, or just a one-off thing. If it's one point of willpower and bang, cured, that seems reasonable.</div> </div> </div> </div>My understanding is that the next time you have the opportunity to exchange sweat with the Wolf-Blooded, you lose a point of Willpower if for some reason you can't or they won't. It also says you lose it &quot;until the Wolf-Blooded willingly engages in the activity&quot;, so I assume the Willpower doesn't come back until you exchange sweat with them again. You don't have to continue spending Willpower to resist future opportunities after the first, but you don't get your Willpower back until you get them to do it with you again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T08:15:12-07:00","id":529967,"title":"","content":"Isn't that more or less the same as temporarily losing a willpower <i>dot</i> though? That seems... excessive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T08:43:23-07:00","id":529998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/525271-some-questions-concerning-tells?p=529967#post529967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't that more or less the same as temporarily losing a willpower <i>dot</i> though? That seems... excessive.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, it seems pretty extreme, but that seems to me to be what the RaW says. I'm with ChanceTR though, I think a temporary version of the Addicted Condition would work much better than this floating mechanic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T09:18:25-07:00","id":530036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/525271-some-questions-concerning-tells?p=529998#post529998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree, it seems pretty extreme, but that seems to me to be what the RaW says. I'm with ChanceTR though, I think a temporary version of the Addicted Condition would work much better than this floating mechanic.</div> </div> </div> </div>It looks like something editing overlooked. No biggie, IMO, considering how tiny the space for individual tells are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T09:42:26-07:00","id":530063,"title":"","content":"I'm still not entirely sure how Shadow Twin is supposed to work. Is your twin a spirit? Do they also need to be at a locus to cross over? Can they also cross at will, dragging you into the shadow? Can they be killed? What happens if they are? <br /> <br /> It's a neat idea but there are just so many loose ends...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T09:56:42-07:00","id":530078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/525271-some-questions-concerning-tells?p=530063#post530063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm still not entirely sure how Shadow Twin is supposed to work. <br /> It's a neat idea but there are just so many loose ends...</div> </div> </div> </div>This is something you should discuss with your ST, clearly. Personally, I would go like this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/525271-some-questions-concerning-tells?p=530063#post530063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is your twin a spirit?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, yes it is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/525271-some-questions-concerning-tells?p=530063#post530063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do they also need to be at a locus to cross over?</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Bold\"><b>Boon</b><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">: <b>At a locus</b>, you and she may switch places, allowing you to Reach.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/525271-some-questions-concerning-tells?p=530063#post530063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can they also cross at will, dragging you into the shadow?</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a manifestation or numen that allows spirits to drag people into the shadow. Would make for a cool story hook.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/525271-some-questions-concerning-tells?p=530063#post530063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can they be killed? What happens if they are?</div> </div> </div> </div>The spirit twin would discorporate and your existence would regenerate it. Or you lose your tell and develop another one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T21:15:59-07:00","id":530624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/525271-some-questions-concerning-tells?p=529998#post529998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree, it seems pretty extreme, but that seems to me to be what the RaW says. I'm with ChanceTR though, I think a temporary version of the Addicted Condition would work much better than this floating mechanic.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Right, and at least this way you can get beats out of it somehow. <br /> <br /> As far as the Shadow Twin thing goes, I wouldn't think that both of them would need to be at the locus. At least, that's not how I would run it in my stories. I would allow the transferance while one or the other is there, otherwise the Shadow Twin could simply take over your body and never come back, which isn't much of a boon. I'd rule that as long as one of them is at a locus and wants to cross, the transferance takes place, that way there is at least some drama. If the shadow twin wants to take over, it would have to set a trap, which still leaves the character some agency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5309-chancetr","name":"ChanceTR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5309_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-30T18:53:12-07:00","id":533878,"title":"","content":"So here's one for you: Does a familiar, and thus his werewolf, take damage every single time an attack is made against either of them, or just the first time in the scene? It seems ambiguous. Like, does one damage transfer at just the start of the right, or every time one of them gets hit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5309-chancetr","name":"ChanceTR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5309_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-30T19:23:09-07:00","id":533898,"title":"","content":"It seems pretty clear. 'Each time the familiar is damaged, the Wolf-Blooded takes the first point of damage instead of the familiar.' So every time an attack is made against the familiar and likewise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}